ation during that period.\r\n\r\n2. Duration of Probation\r\nAll new full-time employees serve a probation period of 3 months (90 calendar days) from their date of joining, unless a different duration is explicitly stated in their offer letter.\r\n\r\n3. Notice Period During Probation\n\n[Source: probation_policy.txt] (relevance: 0.59)\n6. Extension of Probation\r\nIn cases where performance is inconclusive rather than clearly unsatisfactory, the probation period may be extended by up to 2 additional months at the manager's discretion, with written justification shared with the employee and HR. An extension is not a guarantee of eventual confirmation.\r\n\r\n7. Benefits During Probation\n\n[Source: notice_period_policy.txt] (relevance: 0.57)\n2. Standard Notice Period\r\nOnce an employee has been confirmed after probation (see the Probation Policy), the standard notice period is 60 days (2 calendar months) for both resignation by the employee and termination initiated by the company, except in cases of termination for cause.\r\n\r\n3. Notice Period for Senior Roles\n\n[Source: probation_policy.txt] (relevance: 0.50)\n3. Notice Period During Probation\r\nDuring the probation period, either the employee or the company may terminate the employment relationship with 15 days' written notice, or payment in lieu of notice, whichever the terminating party elects. This is shorter than the standard post-confirmation notice period described in the Notice Period Policy.\r\n\r\n4. Performance Review During Probation\n\n[Source: probation_policy.txt] (relevance: 0.43)\n4. Performance Review During Probation\r\nEmployees on probation receive a formal check-in with their manager at the 6-week mark and a final review before the end of the 3-month period. The final review assesses role competency, cultural fit, and alignment with team expectations.\r\n\r\n5. Confirmation", name='search_hr_policy', id='a3ed2265-0f57-484c-847f-e1fd323cf0e3', tool_call_id='call_5439623c705a44b3b7266d1d9935__thought__'), AIMessage(content='The standard probation period for all new full-time employees is 3 months (90 calendar days) from their date of joining, unless a different duration is explicitly stated in their offer letter.\n\n[Source: probation_policy.txt]', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'thought_signatures': ['']}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=133, prompt_tokens=1171, total_tokens=1304, completion_tokens_details=CompletionTokensDetailsWrapper(accepted_prediction_tokens=None, audio_tokens=None, reasoning_tokens=84, rejected_prediction_tokens=None, text_tokens=49, image_tokens=None, video_tokens=None), prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetailsWrapper(audio_tokens=None, cached_tokens=None, text_tokens=1171, image_tokens=None, video_tokens=None), cache_read_input_tokens=None), 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'model_name': 'hr-llm', 'model_provider': 'litellm', 'model_id': 'ea9549931e74c4222186635978c3c226571e50284cb4a083fcf148f22659f009', 'response_cost': 0.0006838}, id='lc_run--01a17375-9456-7e52-99e8-65bcdbdf8e4c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1171, 'output_tokens': 133, 'total_tokens': 1304, 'output_token_details': {'reasoning': 84}})]}
