2026-10-25 19:58:02,738 | INFO     | [File: vector_store.py] [Method: get_retriever] [Line: 154] | Entering get_retriever() with k=12, filter_categories={'Exit Process', 'Leave', 'Probation', 'Code of Conduct', 'Holidays', 'Maternity Paternity', 'Reimbursement', 'Work From Home', 'Notice Period', 'Travel Expense'}
2026-10-25 19:58:04,110 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank_with_scores] [Line: 26] | Entering rerank_with_scores() with query: How many paid sick days do I get per year?, candidates: ['3. Sick Leave\r\nEmployees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. Sick leave does not carry forward to the following year. For sick leave of 3 or more consecutive days, a medical certificate must be submitted to HR within 5 working days of returning to work.\r\n\r\n4. Casual Leave', '2. Annual Paid Leave\r\nEvery full-time employee is entitled to 18 days of paid annual leave per calendar year, accrued at a rate of 1.5 days per completed month of service. Unused annual leave may be carried forward to the next calendar year up to a maximum of 10 days; any balance beyond that is forfeited on December 31st unless local law requires otherwise.\r\n\r\n3. Sick Leave', '4. Casual Leave\r\nEmployees may take up to 6 days of casual leave per calendar year for personal matters that do not qualify as sick leave, such as family emergencies or personal errands. Casual leave requests should ideally be submitted at least 1 working day in advance, though same-day requests are accepted for genuine emergencies.\r\n\r\n5. How to Apply for Leave', "3. Floating Holidays\r\nIn addition to the 12 fixed public holidays, employees receive 2 floating holidays per year, which can be used on any working day of the employee's choosing (for example, to observe a cultural or religious holiday not included in the standard list). Floating holidays must be requested through the HR portal at least 2 working days in advance and do not carry forward to the next year.\r\n\r\n4. Holidays Falling on a Weekend", "PUBLIC HOLIDAYS POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Holidays\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy lists the public holidays observed by the company each calendar year and how they interact with other leave types.\r\n\r\n2. Number of Observed Holidays\r\nThe company observes 12 public holidays per calendar year, published on the HR portal by December 1st of the preceding year. The list is based on national and regional holidays for the employee's registered work location.\r\n\r\n3. Floating Holidays", "3. Paternity Leave\r\nEmployees whose partner gives birth are entitled to 2 weeks of paid paternity leave, to be taken within 3 months of the child's birth. Paternity leave may be split into two blocks with manager approval.\r\n\r\n4. Adoption Leave\r\nAn employee who legally adopts a child under the age of 1 year is entitled to 12 weeks of paid adoption leave, starting from the date the child is placed with the employee.\r\n\r\n5. Notification Requirements", "5. How to Apply for Leave\r\nAll leave requests must be submitted through the internal HR portal at least 3 working days in advance for planned leave (annual and casual leave). Sick leave may be reported on the day of absence and formalized in the portal upon return. Leave requests are approved by the employee's direct manager and are subject to team workload and business needs.\r\n\r\n6. Leave During Notice Period", "7. Unpaid Leave\r\nIn exceptional circumstances, employees who have exhausted their paid leave balance may request unpaid leave. Unpaid leave requests must be approved by both the direct manager and HR, and require at least 5 working days' notice except in emergencies.\r\n\r\n8. Public Holidays\r\nLeave taken on a day that is already a declared public holiday (see the Public Holidays Policy) is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance.", '3. Standard Work From Home Allowance\r\nEligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week as a standing arrangement, agreed with their manager. Employees are not permitted to work from home every day as a default arrangement; teams are expected to maintain in-office collaboration on at least 3 days per week unless the role is designated fully remote in the employment contract.\r\n\r\n4. Occasional Work From Home', '5. Professional Development Reimbursement\r\nEmployees may claim up to 25,000 (local currency) per calendar year toward job-relevant certifications or courses, subject to prior manager approval before enrollment. Reimbursement is processed only after successful completion of the course or certification.\r\n\r\n6. Submission Process', '6. Per Diem Allowance\r\nEmployees on approved business travel receive a daily per-diem allowance covering meals and incidental expenses, at a rate published on the HR portal, varying by destination country. Per diem is paid regardless of actual spend and does not require receipts.\r\n\r\n7. Ground Transportation', '5. Working on a Public Holiday\r\nEmployees required to work on a declared public holiday due to business needs (e.g., customer support coverage) are entitled to a compensatory day off within 30 days, in addition to any applicable holiday pay as required by local law.\r\n\r\n6. Interaction With Annual Leave'], top_n: 5
