\n\r\n6. Extension of Probation", '6. Leave During Notice Period\r\nEmployees serving their notice period (see the Notice Period Policy) may not take annual leave during the last 15 days of their notice period without explicit written approval from their manager and HR.\r\n\r\n7. Unpaid Leave', '9. Probationary Employees\r\nEmployees on probation (see the Probation Policy) who become eligible for maternity, paternity, or adoption leave during their probation period have their probation period paused and resumed upon return, rather than counted against them.', '3. Notice Period for Senior Roles\r\nEmployees at the Director level and above are required to serve a notice period of 90 days, given the additional handover and succession planning typically required at that level.\r\n\r\n4. Payment in Lieu of Notice', '6. Leave During Notice Period\r\nAs stated in the Leave Policy, annual leave may not be taken during the final 15 days of the notice period without written approval from both the manager and HR, to ensure adequate handover time.\r\n\r\n7. Termination for Cause', "6. Extension of Probation\r\nIn cases where performance is inconclusive rather than clearly unsatisfactory, the probation period may be extended by up to 2 additional months at the manager's discretion, with written justification shared with the employee and HR. An extension is not a guarantee of eventual confirmation.\r\n\r\n7. Benefits During Probation", "4. Payment in Lieu of Notice\r\nEither party may elect to shorten the notice period through payment in lieu of notice. If the company initiates this, the employee receives their full salary and benefits for the unserved portion of the notice period. If the employee requests early release and the company agrees, the employee may be required to forfeit salary for the unserved period, at the company's discretion.\r\n\r\n5. Handover Requirements", '4. Performance Review During Probation\r\nEmployees on probation receive a formal check-in with their manager at the 6-week mark and a final review before the end of the 3-month period. The final review assesses role competency, cultural fit, and alignment with team expectations.\r\n\r\n5. Confirmation'], top_n: 5
