2026-10-25 19:59:16,793 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank_with_scores] [Line: 26] | Entering rerank_with_scores() with query: Within how many days must reimbursement claims be submitted?, candidates: ['6. Submission Process\r\nAll reimbursement claims must be submitted through the finance portal within 30 days of the expense being incurred, with original receipts or digital invoices attached. Claims submitted after 30 days may be rejected at the discretion of the finance team.\r\n\r\n7. Approval Workflow\r\nClaims under 5,000 (local currency) require only direct manager approval. Claims of 5,000 or more require both manager and finance department approval before reimbursement is processed.', '9. Expense Submission Deadline\r\nAll trip-related expenses must be submitted within 15 days of returning from travel, shorter than the standard 30-day window in the general Reimbursement Policy, due to the higher volume and time-sensitivity of travel claims.', '7. Final Settlement\r\nThe final settlement, including any pending salary, unused annual leave encashment (up to the carry-forward limit defined in the Leave Policy), and reimbursement of approved pending claims, is processed within 45 days of the last working day, in line with standard payroll cycles.\r\n\r\n8. Full and Final Documents', '8. Non-Reimbursable Items\r\nPersonal expenses, fines or penalties, alcohol (except in pre-approved client entertainment contexts), and any expense without a valid receipt are not eligible for reimbursement.\r\n\r\n9. Payment Timeline\r\nApproved reimbursements are paid out with the next regular payroll cycle following approval, typically within 15 working days.', '3. Sick Leave\r\nEmployees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. Sick leave does not carry forward to the following year. For sick leave of 3 or more consecutive days, a medical certificate must be submitted to HR within 5 working days of returning to work.\r\n\r\n4. Casual Leave', '5. Professional Development Reimbursement\r\nEmployees may claim up to 25,000 (local currency) per calendar year toward job-relevant certifications or courses, subject to prior manager approval before enrollment. Reimbursement is processed only after successful completion of the course or certification.\r\n\r\n6. Submission Process', 'REIMBURSEMENT POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Reimbursement\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy explains which work-related expenses employees may claim reimbursement for, the applicable limits, and the submission process.\r\n\r\n2. Eligible Expense Categories', '3. Home Office Setup Allowance\r\nEmployees eligible for the Work From Home Policy may claim a one-time home office setup allowance of up to 15,000 (local currency) within their first 3 months of eligibility, covering items such as a desk, chair, or monitor. Receipts are required for all claims.\r\n\r\n4. Internet and Mobile Reimbursement', "EXIT PROCESS POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Exit Process\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy describes the steps an employee and the company follow between resignation (or termination) and the employee's last working day.\r\n\r\n2. Resignation Submission\r\nEmployees who wish to resign must submit their resignation in writing through the HR portal, triggering the notice period described in the Notice Period Policy. The resignation is acknowledged by the manager and HR within 3 working days.\r\n\r\n3. Exit Interview", '4. Internet and Mobile Reimbursement\r\nEmployees with a standing work-from-home arrangement may claim up to 1,500 (local currency) per month toward internet costs, and up to 1,000 (local currency) per month toward mobile bills, provided these are used substantially for work purposes.\r\n\r\n5. Professional Development Reimbursement', "2. Eligible Expense Categories\r\nThe following categories are eligible for reimbursement, subject to the limits below: internet and mobile bills for remote work, home office setup (one-time), professional certifications relevant to the employee's role, business travel (see also the Travel and Expense Policy for trip-specific rules), and client entertainment pre-approved by a manager.\r\n\r\n3. Home Office Setup Allowance", "5. How to Apply for Leave\r\nAll leave requests must be submitted through the internal HR portal at least 3 working days in advance for planned leave (annual and casual leave). Sick leave may be reported on the day of absence and formalized in the portal upon return. Leave requests are approved by the employee's direct manager and are subject to team workload and business needs.\r\n\r\n6. Leave During Notice Period"], top_n: 5
