2026-10-25 19:59:53,725 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank] [Line: 53] | Entering rerank() with query: How many days of unused annual leave can be carried forward?, candidates: ['2. Annual Paid Leave\r\nEvery full-time employee is entitled to 18 days of paid annual leave per calendar year, accrued at a rate of 1.5 days per completed month of service. Unused annual leave may be carried forward to the next calendar year up to a maximum of 10 days; any balance beyond that is forfeited on December 31st unless local law requires otherwise.\r\n\r\n3. Sick Leave', "7. Unpaid Leave\r\nIn exceptional circumstances, employees who have exhausted their paid leave balance may request unpaid leave. Unpaid leave requests must be approved by both the direct manager and HR, and require at least 5 working days' notice except in emergencies.\r\n\r\n8. Public Holidays\r\nLeave taken on a day that is already a declared public holiday (see the Public Holidays Policy) is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance.", '3. Sick Leave\r\nEmployees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. Sick leave does not carry forward to the following year. For sick leave of 3 or more consecutive days, a medical certificate must be submitted to HR within 5 working days of returning to work.\r\n\r\n4. Casual Leave', '7. Final Settlement\r\nThe final settlement, including any pending salary, unused annual leave encashment (up to the carry-forward limit defined in the Leave Policy), and reimbursement of approved pending claims, is processed within 45 days of the last working day, in line with standard payroll cycles.\r\n\r\n8. Full and Final Documents', '6. Leave During Notice Period\r\nAs stated in the Leave Policy, annual leave may not be taken during the final 15 days of the notice period without written approval from both the manager and HR, to ensure adequate handover time.\r\n\r\n7. Termination for Cause', "6. Interaction With Annual Leave\r\nAs noted in the Leave Policy, a public holiday that falls within a period of approved annual leave is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance; the leave balance is automatically adjusted.\r\n\r\n7. Office Closure\r\nThe office (for employees not working from home) is closed on all declared public holidays. Employees working from home on such days are not expected to be reachable, the same as employees in the office.\r\n\r\n8. Regional Variations", "5. How to Apply for Leave\r\nAll leave requests must be submitted through the internal HR portal at least 3 working days in advance for planned leave (annual and casual leave). Sick leave may be reported on the day of absence and formalized in the portal upon return. Leave requests are approved by the employee's direct manager and are subject to team workload and business needs.\r\n\r\n6. Leave During Notice Period", '6. Leave During Notice Period\r\nEmployees serving their notice period (see the Notice Period Policy) may not take annual leave during the last 15 days of their notice period without explicit written approval from their manager and HR.\r\n\r\n7. Unpaid Leave', '4. Casual Leave\r\nEmployees may take up to 6 days of casual leave per calendar year for personal matters that do not qualify as sick leave, such as family emergencies or personal errands. Casual leave requests should ideally be submitted at least 1 working day in advance, though same-day requests are accepted for genuine emergencies.\r\n\r\n5. How to Apply for Leave', "3. Floating Holidays\r\nIn addition to the 12 fixed public holidays, employees receive 2 floating holidays per year, which can be used on any working day of the employee's choosing (for example, to observe a cultural or religious holiday not included in the standard list). Floating holidays must be requested through the HR portal at least 2 working days in advance and do not carry forward to the next year.\r\n\r\n4. Holidays Falling on a Weekend", '5. Working on a Public Holiday\r\nEmployees required to work on a declared public holiday due to business needs (e.g., customer support coverage) are entitled to a compensatory day off within 30 days, in addition to any applicable holiday pay as required by local law.\r\n\r\n6. Interaction With Annual Leave', '2. Maternity Leave\r\nEmployees who give birth are entitled to 26 weeks of paid maternity leave, which may begin up to 8 weeks before the expected delivery date. This entitlement applies to employees who have completed at least 80 days of service in the 12 months preceding the expected delivery date.\r\n\r\n3. Paternity Leave'], top_n: 5
