2026-10-25 20:00:09,049 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank_with_scores] [Line: 26] | Entering rerank_with_scores() with query: How many public holidays does the company observe each year?, candidates: ["PUBLIC HOLIDAYS POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Holidays\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy lists the public holidays observed by the company each calendar year and how they interact with other leave types.\r\n\r\n2. Number of Observed Holidays\r\nThe company observes 12 public holidays per calendar year, published on the HR portal by December 1st of the preceding year. The list is based on national and regional holidays for the employee's registered work location.\r\n\r\n3. Floating Holidays", "3. Floating Holidays\r\nIn addition to the 12 fixed public holidays, employees receive 2 floating holidays per year, which can be used on any working day of the employee's choosing (for example, to observe a cultural or religious holiday not included in the standard list). Floating holidays must be requested through the HR portal at least 2 working days in advance and do not carry forward to the next year.\r\n\r\n4. Holidays Falling on a Weekend", "6. Interaction With Annual Leave\r\nAs noted in the Leave Policy, a public holiday that falls within a period of approved annual leave is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance; the leave balance is automatically adjusted.\r\n\r\n7. Office Closure\r\nThe office (for employees not working from home) is closed on all declared public holidays. Employees working from home on such days are not expected to be reachable, the same as employees in the office.\r\n\r\n8. Regional Variations", '4. Holidays Falling on a Weekend\r\nIf a public holiday falls on a weekend, it is generally not shifted to the nearest working day unless explicitly announced by HR for that year, in which case the adjusted date will be published alongside the annual holiday calendar.\r\n\r\n5. Working on a Public Holiday', '5. Working on a Public Holiday\r\nEmployees required to work on a declared public holiday due to business needs (e.g., customer support coverage) are entitled to a compensatory day off within 30 days, in addition to any applicable holiday pay as required by local law.\r\n\r\n6. Interaction With Annual Leave', "7. Unpaid Leave\r\nIn exceptional circumstances, employees who have exhausted their paid leave balance may request unpaid leave. Unpaid leave requests must be approved by both the direct manager and HR, and require at least 5 working days' notice except in emergencies.\r\n\r\n8. Public Holidays\r\nLeave taken on a day that is already a declared public holiday (see the Public Holidays Policy) is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance.", '8. Regional Variations\r\nEmployees based in different regions or countries may observe a different holiday list appropriate to their location; HR publishes a location-specific calendar for each office.', '2. Annual Paid Leave\r\nEvery full-time employee is entitled to 18 days of paid annual leave per calendar year, accrued at a rate of 1.5 days per completed month of service. Unused annual leave may be carried forward to the next calendar year up to a maximum of 10 days; any balance beyond that is forfeited on December 31st unless local law requires otherwise.\r\n\r\n3. Sick Leave', '8. Consequences of Violation\r\nViolations of this Code of Conduct may result in disciplinary action up to and including termination for cause, as referenced in the Notice Period Policy, depending on the severity and nature of the violation.\r\n\r\n9. Social Media and Public Statements\r\nEmployees should avoid making public statements on behalf of the company without authorization, and should exercise good judgment when posting about work-related topics on personal social media accounts.', 'CODE OF CONDUCT POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Code of Conduct\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy sets out the standards of behavior expected of every employee, contractor, and manager while representing the company.\r\n\r\n2. Core Principles\r\nAll employees are expected to act with honesty, respect, and professionalism in every interaction, whether with colleagues, clients, partners, or the public, in person or online.\r\n\r\n3. Respect and Non-Discrimination', '4. Casual Leave\r\nEmployees may take up to 6 days of casual leave per calendar year for personal matters that do not qualify as sick leave, such as family emergencies or personal errands. Casual leave requests should ideally be submitted at least 1 working day in advance, though same-day requests are accepted for genuine emergencies.\r\n\r\n5. How to Apply for Leave', '5. Confidentiality\r\nEmployees must not share confidential company information, including client data, financial information, or unreleased product plans, with anyone outside the company without proper authorization, both during and after their employment.\r\n\r\n6. Use of Company Resources'], top_n: 5
