2026-10-25 20:00:27,337 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank_with_scores] [Line: 26] | Entering rerank_with_scores() with query: What is the standard notice period for a confirmed employee?, candidates: ['2. Standard Notice Period\r\nOnce an employee has been confirmed after probation (see the Probation Policy), the standard notice period is 60 days (2 calendar months) for both resignation by the employee and termination initiated by the company, except in cases of termination for cause.\r\n\r\n3. Notice Period for Senior Roles', 'NOTICE PERIOD POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Notice Period\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy defines the notice period required when an employee resigns or when the company initiates termination of employment, outside of the probation period.\r\n\r\n2. Standard Notice Period', "5. Confirmation\r\nIf performance during probation is satisfactory, the employee's manager submits a confirmation recommendation to HR before the end of the probation period. Once confirmed, the employee moves to the standard notice period and full leave entitlements described elsewhere in this handbook.\r\n\r\n6. Extension of Probation", "3. Notice Period During Probation\r\nDuring the probation period, either the employee or the company may terminate the employment relationship with 15 days' written notice, or payment in lieu of notice, whichever the terminating party elects. This is shorter than the standard post-confirmation notice period described in the Notice Period Policy.\r\n\r\n4. Performance Review During Probation", '3. Notice Period for Senior Roles\r\nEmployees at the Director level and above are required to serve a notice period of 90 days, given the additional handover and succession planning typically required at that level.\r\n\r\n4. Payment in Lieu of Notice', 'PROBATION POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Probation\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy describes the probation period applicable to new employees and the process for confirmation, extension, or termination during that period.\r\n\r\n2. Duration of Probation\r\nAll new full-time employees serve a probation period of 3 months (90 calendar days) from their date of joining, unless a different duration is explicitly stated in their offer letter.\r\n\r\n3. Notice Period During Probation', '6. Leave During Notice Period\r\nEmployees serving their notice period (see the Notice Period Policy) may not take annual leave during the last 15 days of their notice period without explicit written approval from their manager and HR.\r\n\r\n7. Unpaid Leave', "4. Payment in Lieu of Notice\r\nEither party may elect to shorten the notice period through payment in lieu of notice. If the company initiates this, the employee receives their full salary and benefits for the unserved portion of the notice period. If the employee requests early release and the company agrees, the employee may be required to forfeit salary for the unserved period, at the company's discretion.\r\n\r\n5. Handover Requirements", '5. Notification Requirements\r\nEmployees should notify HR and their manager of their expected leave at least 8 weeks in advance where possible, to allow for adequate handover and temporary coverage planning, coordinated similarly to the handover process in the Notice Period Policy.\r\n\r\n6. Job Protection', '5. Handover Requirements\r\nDuring the notice period, the departing employee is expected to prepare a written handover document covering ongoing projects, key contacts, and access credentials, to be reviewed with their manager no later than 10 days before the last working day.\r\n\r\n6. Leave During Notice Period', '7. Termination for Cause\r\nIn cases of termination for cause (e.g., serious misconduct, breach of the Code of Conduct Policy), the standard notice period does not apply, and termination may be immediate, subject to applicable local labor law and internal disciplinary procedures.\r\n\r\n8. Exit Formalities\r\nAll notice period completions are followed by the formal exit process described in the Exit Process Policy, including final settlement, asset return, and exit interview.', '8. Full and Final Documents\r\nHR issues a relieving letter and experience certificate to the employee within 10 working days of the last working day, provided all handover and asset return requirements have been completed.\r\n\r\n9. Rehire Eligibility\r\nEmployees who leave in good standing, having completed the full exit process, remain eligible for future rehire consideration, subject to standard hiring processes at the time.'], top_n: 5
