2026-10-25 20:15:43,359 | INFO     | [File: reranker.py] [Method: rerank_with_scores] [Line: 26] | Entering rerank_with_scores() with query: How many days per week can I work from home?, candidates: ['3. Standard Work From Home Allowance\r\nEligible employees may work from home up to 2 days per week as a standing arrangement, agreed with their manager. Employees are not permitted to work from home every day as a default arrangement; teams are expected to maintain in-office collaboration on at least 3 days per week unless the role is designated fully remote in the employment contract.\r\n\r\n4. Occasional Work From Home', '4. Occasional Work From Home\r\nIn addition to the standing 2-day allowance, employees may request occasional additional work-from-home days (e.g., for a home repair appointment or a focus-heavy task) by informing their manager at least 1 day in advance via chat or email. These occasional requests are not tracked formally but should be reasonable in frequency.\r\n\r\n5. Fully Remote Roles', '7. Expectations While Working From Home\r\nEmployees working from home are expected to be reachable during standard working hours, attend scheduled meetings with video on where appropriate, and maintain the same productivity standards as in-office work. Repeated unavailability during working hours while marked as "working from home" may result in the arrangement being revoked.\r\n\r\n8. Manager Discretion', '4. Internet and Mobile Reimbursement\r\nEmployees with a standing work-from-home arrangement may claim up to 1,500 (local currency) per month toward internet costs, and up to 1,000 (local currency) per month toward mobile bills, provided these are used substantially for work purposes.\r\n\r\n5. Professional Development Reimbursement', 'WORK FROM HOME POLICY\r\n\r\nPolicy Category: Work From Home\r\n\r\n1. Purpose\r\nThis policy outlines the eligibility, expectations, and process for employees working remotely on a regular or occasional basis.\r\n\r\n2. Eligibility\r\nEmployees who have completed their probation period (see the Probation Policy) and whose role does not require a fixed physical presence (e.g., front-desk, warehouse, or facilities roles) are eligible to work from home, subject to manager approval.', '4. Casual Leave\r\nEmployees may take up to 6 days of casual leave per calendar year for personal matters that do not qualify as sick leave, such as family emergencies or personal errands. Casual leave requests should ideally be submitted at least 1 working day in advance, though same-day requests are accepted for genuine emergencies.\r\n\r\n5. How to Apply for Leave', '3. Sick Leave\r\nEmployees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. Sick leave does not carry forward to the following year. For sick leave of 3 or more consecutive days, a medical certificate must be submitted to HR within 5 working days of returning to work.\r\n\r\n4. Casual Leave', "8. Manager Discretion\r\nTeam managers retain discretion to temporarily suspend work-from-home arrangements for specific projects that require in-person collaboration, with at least 1 week's notice to affected employees where possible.", "3. Floating Holidays\r\nIn addition to the 12 fixed public holidays, employees receive 2 floating holidays per year, which can be used on any working day of the employee's choosing (for example, to observe a cultural or religious holiday not included in the standard list). Floating holidays must be requested through the HR portal at least 2 working days in advance and do not carry forward to the next year.\r\n\r\n4. Holidays Falling on a Weekend", '3. Home Office Setup Allowance\r\nEmployees eligible for the Work From Home Policy may claim a one-time home office setup allowance of up to 15,000 (local currency) within their first 3 months of eligibility, covering items such as a desk, chair, or monitor. Receipts are required for all claims.\r\n\r\n4. Internet and Mobile Reimbursement', '6. Equipment and Expenses\r\nThe company provides a laptop and any role-specific software required to work from home. A one-time home office setup allowance may be claimed through the Reimbursement Policy, subject to the limits defined there.\r\n\r\n7. Expectations While Working From Home', "6. Interaction With Annual Leave\r\nAs noted in the Leave Policy, a public holiday that falls within a period of approved annual leave is not deducted from the employee's annual leave balance; the leave balance is automatically adjusted.\r\n\r\n7. Office Closure\r\nThe office (for employees not working from home) is closed on all declared public holidays. Employees working from home on such days are not expected to be reachable, the same as employees in the office.\r\n\r\n8. Regional Variations"], top_n: 5
